{"title":"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that there exists a positive constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that the following statement is true:\n</p><p>Consider an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, and a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of n points in the plane such that the distance between any two different points in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. It follows that there is a line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> separating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> such that the distance from any point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/2/b4230a1da55c102ea35bbdf99082e3b24291de9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cn^{- \\frac{1}{3}}$\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>(A line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> separates a set of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> if some segment joining two points in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> crosses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />.)\n</p><p><i>Note</i>. Weaker results with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/2/b4230a1da55c102ea35bbdf99082e3b24291de9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cn^{- \\frac{1}{3}}$\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> replaced by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb308290f052416a7b7db7f46f06b588f7ff69ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cn^{- \\alpha}$\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" /> may be awarded points depending on the value\nof the constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1dcc1ecb7ad66843e62c9693361f4765e31bfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha &gt; \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any unit vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c9443f88d30aadea70186fd39d3763995198922e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_v=\\min_{p\\in S} p \\cdot v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"25\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/3060d8406c7043fd676d8606fb0af61a814734ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_v = \\max_{p\\in S} p\\cdot v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"25\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2e874b07c2270fe16d7317f1b00e80fe5f12d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_v - a_v\\geq n^{2/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"21\" /> then we can find a line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> separates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and any point in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/101bbdb8f48ec8c92a0d6a1d3be2063f21492ee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega(n^{2/3}/n) = \\Omega(n^{-1/3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"23\" /> away from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose there is no such direction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is contained in a box with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b7281da71446cbe56a9d08b71243f01d73b4133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2/3}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> by considering the direction of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/754e946d1a160f767f0f61cbd9460401c2d1c17f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6457ca2dcd40dc21d9aa0db18c66bbac9af4d899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is contained in a disk with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b7281da71446cbe56a9d08b71243f01d73b4133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2/3}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />. Now suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the disk with the minimum radius, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, which contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/8/3c819490a99aa8dd50a5097f149627be514f21ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=O(n^{2/3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" />. Since the distance between any two points in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c752c2fba60d94266f334b5c79aac6b80a948ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\Omega(\\sqrt{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" /> too.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be any point in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> on the boundary of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff9d2add1273f7f294d4f0318b0ed4340c07768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> be the line tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a3f7a0a3b548d0684d391994a6366f8d71ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> the line obtained by translating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff9d2add1273f7f294d4f0318b0ed4340c07768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> by distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> towards the inside of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the region sandwiched by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff9d2add1273f7f294d4f0318b0ed4340c07768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a3f7a0a3b548d0684d391994a6366f8d71ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" />. It is easy to show that both the area and the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/2/c02b552a94194a87c3723c3660555bd1382d0423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H\\cap D$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> is bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd2e96e7cda56037592fab124f1c5b7e26eb463e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O(\\sqrt{r})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"19\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c752c2fba60d94266f334b5c79aac6b80a948ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\Omega(\\sqrt{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" />). Hence, there can only be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1656a3164b38b5b94efe58ffbdca9d0619e033.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O(\\sqrt{r})=O(n^{1/3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" /> points in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/4/664e35f78cb5c9a63af555d8c7e1ab96c4575cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H\\cap S$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />, by that any two points in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apart. Since the width of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there must exist a line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff9d2add1273f7f294d4f0318b0ed4340c07768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> separates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and any point in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80df72e99ed291963d9feaacdbc41b8fe5844d44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/O(n^{1/3}) = \\Omega(n^{-1/3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" /> away from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />.  Q.E.D.\n</p><p>Note. One can also show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/5/02594e72de3a85cad1436f9d9419997ac2fd27b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega(n^{-1/3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> is best possible.\n~Shen Kislay kai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTqwOoSfaAA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTqwOoSfaAA</a> [video covers all day 2 problems]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO\" title=\"2020 IMO\">2020 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018013100\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 395/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 866/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 12567/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.146      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.146      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19753:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018013100 and revision id 226305. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}